!!id:"https://schemas.example.com/2026/40/orders/orders-api-secured-1.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/io/ltr8/http/http.tn"
!!import:"https://schemas.example.com/2026/40/orders/orders-1.tn"
@doc:"""
  Security schemes: the protocol of orders-1.tn bound again, each endpoint stating how a client proves who it
  is. A scheme is a value entry at the root, tagged with the kind of scheme it is, and a projection or an
  endpoint names it in `security`, a reference the resolver judges, so a name that is no scheme fails at load.

  The projection's `security` is the default. An endpoint writing its own replaces it, and an endpoint writing
  `security: []` is open; one writing none inherits. The schemes in force, as the reader resolves them:

    POST   /orders        bearer                    inherited from the projection
    GET    /orders        partner_key               replaced
    GET    /orders/{id}   (open)                    `security: []`
    DELETE /orders/{id}   bearer, partner_key       replaced; a credential for either one will do

  The description states a scheme and the reader reads it; nothing enforces one.
  """
!schema {
  @doc:"A bearer token (RFC 6750), sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`."
  bearer => !http.auth { scheme: Bearer }

  @doc:"A key issued to a partner, sent in the `X-Api-Key` header."
  partner_key => !http.api_key { in: header  name: "X-Api-Key" }

  orders_http => !http.projection {
    binds: [orders]
    security: [bearer]
    resources: {
      "/orders" => {
        POST => !http.binding { exchange: orders.exchanges.place_order  status: 201 }
        GET  => !http.binding { exchange: orders.exchanges.list_orders  security: [partner_key] }
      }
      "/orders/{id}" => {
        GET    => !http.binding { exchange: orders.exchanges.get_order  security: []
                                  response_headers: { Cache-Control => "private, max-age=60" } }
        DELETE => !http.binding { exchange: orders.exchanges.cancel_order  status: 204
                                  security: [bearer partner_key] }
      }
    }
  }
}
